course: dictionary
lesson: 7983
title: A recording is kept to play again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A recording is sound or pictures that have been stored so they can be played again. A song, a video or a voice message can all be recordings. «The Grammy Awards are voted on by members of the Recording Academy, people who work in music, not by fans.» Here Recording is part of a name, so it starts with a capital letter.
explain: Recording can also be a verb. It means storing sound or pictures, so «She is recording a song» means she is storing the song as it is made. In science, recording means writing down results clearly, such as measurements in a table.
explain: Use context to work out the meaning. «One politician said «I never said that!» and a reporter played a recording where he did.» The word played tells you a recording is something you can play back, so it must be stored sound or pictures.
fact: A recording is sound or pictures that have been stored so they can be played again.
fact: Recording as a verb means storing sound or pictures, as in «She is recording a song.»
fact: In science, recording means writing results down clearly, such as in a table or chart.
fact: «A video recording» and «a sound recording» are common phrases.
fact: A «recording studio» is a room where music is recorded.
exercise: «The reporter played a recording of the speech.» What is a recording? | A room with no windows | *Sound or pictures stored so they can be played again | A school bell | A kind of paper
exercise: In science class, Mia is recording the height of her bean plants in a table. What is she doing? | Taking a photo of her friends | Painting a picture | *Writing down results clearly | Singing a song
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that shows someone is storing sound now: «Ella is recording her voice message for Grandad.» | voice | Ella | *recording | Grandad
test: «Some films look like real recordings, but they are still stories.» What does recordings mean here? | Books about the sea | Shouts from a crowd | Stories that are told out loud | *Sound or pictures stored so they can be played again
test: «The recording studio was full of musicians.» What is a recording studio? | A room where people sleep | *A room where music is recorded | A shop that sells shoes | A place for cooking
exam: «Taylor Swift re-recorded her early albums because she wanted to own her music.» Why did she re-record them? | *Because the first recordings were sold without her control | Because she lost her voice | Because the studio was closed | Because the albums were too short
